<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James FitzJames, 1st Duke of Berwick</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1670">1670</a>–<a href="/years/1734">1734</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Duke of Berwick</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James FitzJames, 1st Duke of Berwick, was an illegitimate son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-england">James II of England</a> who became a marshal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a> he won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-almansa">Battle of Almansa</a> in 1707 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> in September 1714 after a long siege. He was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippsburg">Philippsburg</a> in 1734.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-fitzjames-1st-duke-of-berwick.jpg" alt="James FitzJames, 1st Duke of Berwick" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benedetto Gennari II / Formerly attributed to Godfrey Kneller · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Benedetto_Gennari_-_James,_Duke_of_Berwick_-_Alba_Collection.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
